1. DEFINITIONS

"Project" means the Operation Exile: Casino source code and original project files made available by CtrlQuest / Operation Exile.

"Official Workshop Release" means the official Operation Exile: Casino Steam Workshop item published by CtrlQuest / Operation Exile:
https://steamcommunity.com/sharedfiles/filedetails/?id=3803931966

"Derivative Workshop Release" means a separate Steam Workshop upload based in whole or in part on this Project.

"Meaningful Retexture" means genuine original visual customisation of the Project, such as replacement or substantial modification of card artwork, card backs, wheel artwork, slot-machine artwork, UI textures, game artwork, branding, or other visible textures. Changing only a name, logo, metadata, config value, file path, colour value, or a token/minor texture is not a Meaningful Retexture.

2. PERMISSION TO USE AND MODIFY

Subject to this License, you may:

(a) view, study, copy, and modify the Project source code;
(b) use modified or unmodified source code on servers you operate;
(c) create private builds for development, testing, or use on your own DayZ server;
(d) fork the source repository for development and contribution purposes, provided this License and the required attribution are retained; and
(e) create and distribute a Derivative Workshop Release only under the conditions in Section 4.

3. NORMAL SERVER USE

For ordinary public server use, server owners are encouraged to use the Official Workshop Release rather than creating a separate Workshop upload.

Use of the Official Workshop Release on a monetised DayZ server is permitted by this License, provided the server operator complies with all applicable Bohemia Interactive, Steam, platform, and third-party rules. This License does not grant permission to sell the Project itself or to charge specifically for access to the Project, its casino games, its items, or its source code.

4. STEAM WORKSHOP REDISTRIBUTION

You may not upload an unchanged or minimally modified copy of Operation Exile: Casino to the Steam Workshop.

A Derivative Workshop Release is permitted only if all of the following conditions are met:

(a) the release contains a Meaningful Retexture using visual work that you created or have permission to redistribute;
(b) the release is clearly identified as a modified or retextured derivative of Operation Exile: Casino;
(c) it does not present itself as the official Operation Exile: Casino release;
(d) it prominently credits "CtrlQuest / Operation Exile" as the original project creator;
(e) its Workshop description includes a visible link to the Official Workshop Release:
    https://steamcommunity.com/sharedfiles/filedetails/?id=3803931966
(f) its Workshop description includes a visible link to the source repository:
    https://github.com/CtrlQuest/Operation-Exile-Casino
(g) this License, or a clear link to it, is retained with redistributed source covered by this License; and
(h) all third-party asset licences and attribution requirements are independently respected.

Code changes, configuration changes, renaming, repacking, changing metadata, changing only branding, or changing only one insignificant texture are not sufficient by themselves to permit a separate Steam Workshop upload.

5. NO UNCHANGED REPACKS OR MIRRORS

Except for normal source-code forks permitted by Section 2(d), you may not:

(a) repack and publish the complete Project as your own mod;
(b) mirror the complete packaged Workshop mod as a replacement Workshop item;
(c) upload an unchanged or trivially altered PBO/mod package to Steam Workshop; or
(d) claim authorship of the original Operation Exile: Casino project.

